  "details": "I use both a Windows PC and a Mac, and I often work on my Mac when I am away from home. However, when I try to develop a world that includes UdonSharp on my Mac, I get the following error message, preventing me from developing.\n\n```\n\n[UdonSharp] Could not locate VRChat data directory for exception watcher, make sure you have VRChat installed and have run it at least once or turn off exception watching in the UdonSharp project settings.\n\nUnityEngine.Debug:LogError (object)\n\nUdonSharp.UdonSharpUtils:LogError (object) (at Packages/com.vrchat.udonsharp/Editor/UdonSharpUtils.cs:324)\n\nUdonSharpEditor.RuntimeLogWatcher:InitializeScriptLookup () (at Packages/com.vrchat.udonsharp/Editor/UdonSharpRuntimeLogWatcher.cs:78)\n\nUdonSharpEditor.RuntimeLogWatcher:OnEditorUpdate () (at Packages/com.vrchat.udonsharp/Editor/UdonSharpRuntimeLogWatcher.cs:150)\n\nUnityEditor.EditorApplication:Internal_CallUpdateFunctions () (at /Users/bokken/buildslave/unity/build/Editor/Mono/EditorApplication.cs:310)\n\n```\n\nThe message suggests that I should turn off exception watching in the project settings, and while doing so does make it technically possible to develop, it comes with the drawback of not being able to detect exceptions.\n\nI would really appreciate it if it became possible to develop in environments that do not have VRChat installed. In particular, I would be thrilled if development of projects that include UdonSharp becomes feasible on a Mac.",
